# Git and filesystem safety
Do not use destructive commands such as git reset --hard, git clean -fd,
force pushes, forced branch deletion, or broad recursive deletion unless the
user explicitly requests them. Never print, copy, commit, upload, or expose
credentials, private keys, tokens, authentication caches, or production secrets.
